WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.390
AJA HAMMERLY: In
today's Cloud Minute,

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:02.764
I'll show you a
few of the things

00:00:02.764 --> 00:00:05.670
you can do with the Cloud
Natural Language API in Ruby.

00:00:05.670 --> 00:00:08.220
Cloud Natural Language does
syntax analysis, sentiment

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:10.512
analysis, and entity analysis.

00:00:10.512 --> 00:00:11.970
I've already set
up authentication,

00:00:11.970 --> 00:00:14.790
and I've installed the
Google Cloud Language Gem.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:20.090
To use the API, first I need to
require google/cloud/language.

00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:23.040
Now I need to create
a language object,

00:00:23.040 --> 00:00:28.880
some content to analyze,
and a document object.

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:31.340
To call the API, I can
call the annotate method

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.060
on the document.

00:00:34.060 --> 00:00:36.580
To see the positive or
negative sentiment score,

00:00:36.580 --> 00:00:40.660
I call results.sentiment.score.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:42.442
The syntax analysis
provides an array

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:45.025
of tokens, which are the words
or punctuation in your content.

00:00:48.580 --> 00:00:50.680
To see the entities
that the API identified,

00:00:50.680 --> 00:00:52.030
I can do a similar block.

00:00:55.290 --> 00:00:58.020
This is just the surface of
the Natural Language API.

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:01.070
To learn more, check out the
links in the video description.

